  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>SST302 - Normal Distribution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A standardized test has scores that follow a normal distribution with a mean of \({@mu@}\) and a standard deviation of \({@sigma@}\).</p>
<p>Find the probability that a randomly selected student scores above \({@x_val@}\).</p>
<p>Give your answer to 4 decimal places.</p>
<p>Probability = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>We use the standard normal distribution (Z-score) formula:</p>
<p>\[ Z = \frac{X - \mu}{\sigma} \]</p>
<p>Substituting values:</p>
<p>\[ Z = \frac{{@x_val@} - {@mu@}}{{@sigma@}} = \frac{{@x_val - mu@}}{{@sigma@}} = {@z_score@} \]</p>
<p>Using a standard normal table or calculator:</p>
<p>\[ P(Z \le {@z_score@}) \approx {@prob_less@} \]</p>
<p>Thus, the probability of scoring above {@x_val@}:</p>
<p>\[ P(X > {@x_val@}) = 1 - P(Z \le {@z_score@}) = 1 - {@prob_less@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>mu: 10*(rand(10)+45); /* 450 to 540 */
sigma: 5*(rand(8)+16); /* 80 to 115 */
z_raw: (rand(5)+1)*0.5; /* 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5 */
x_val: mu + z_raw*sigma;
z_score: float((x_val - mu)/sigma);
prob_less: float(cdf_normal(x_val, mu, sigma));
ta1: float(1 - prob_less);
</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text></text>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>N({@mu@}, {@sigma@}), P(X > {@x_val@}). Ans: {@ta1@}.</p>]]></text>
    </questionnote>
