<!-- question: 169581 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>SST302 - Poisson Distribution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A hospital receives an average of \({@lambda@}\) emergency cases per hour.</p>
<p>Using the Poisson distribution, find the probability that exactly \({@k@}\) cases occur in an hour.</p>
<p>Give your answer to 4 decimal places.</p>
<p>Probability = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Poisson probability formula:</p>
<p>\[ P(X = k) = \frac{e^{-\lambda} \lambda^k}{k!} \]</p>
<p>where \(\lambda = {@lambda@}\) and \(k = {@k@}\).</p>
<p>Substituting values:</p>
<p>\[ P(X = {@k@}) = \frac{e^{-{@lambda@}} ({@lambda@}^{@k@})}{{@k@}!} \]</p>
<p>\[ = \frac{({@exp(-lambda)@}) ({@lambda^k@})}{{@k!@}} \]</p>
<p>\[ \approx {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
